description: UI copy and user-facing frontend text must be in English
globs: apps/mydraw_app/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---

# Frontend UI language (English)

When creating or editing anything under `apps/mydraw_app/`:

- Use **English** for all user-visible strings: labels, placeholders, buttons, hints, empty states, errors shown in the UI, `aria-label` / `aria-description`, and comments inside Vue templates that mirror copy.
- Keep **Portuguese** for assistant replies and git commit messages per project rules; this rule applies only to **front-end source** in `mydraw_app`.
- If the API returns localized messages, prefer mapping or generic English fallbacks in the client when you control the message path.
